  "response": "Formulation of defined media for carbon monoxide fermentation by Eubacterium limosum KIST612 and the growth characteristics of the bacterium. (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16232686/)\nciteturn39search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; PMID: 16232686 ...   * Water Environment Research Center, Korea Institute of Science and Technology, Seoul 136-791, Korea. ... Phosphate-buffered (PBBM) and carbonate-buffered (CBBM) basal media were used in the formulation of defined media for the cultivation of Eubacterium limosum KIST612 with carbon monoxide (CO) as the sole energy source.\n# Formulation of defined media for carbon monoxide fermentation by Eubacterium limosum KIST612 and the growth characteristics of the bacterium.\n\nJournal of bioscience and bioengineering\n\nPMID: 16232686\n\nPublication date: 1999\n\nVolume: 88\n\nIssue: 6\n\nPages: 682-5\n\n  * PII: S1389-1723(00)87102-9\n  * DOI: 10.1016/s1389-1723(00)87102-9\n\n## Authors\n\n  * I S Chang\n  * B H Kim\n  * D H Kim\n  * R W Lovitt\n  * H C Sung\n\n\n  * Water Environment Research Center, Korea Institute of Science and Technology, Seoul 136-791, Korea.\n\n## Languages\n\n  * eng\n\n## Publication types\n\n  * Journal Article\n\n## Abstract\n\nPhosphate-buffered (PBBM) and carbonate-buffered (CBBM) basal media were used in the formulation of defined media for the cultivation of Eubacterium limosum KIST612 with carbon monoxide (CO) as the sole energy source. The bacterium was adapted to the minimal media by sequential passage in media containing casamino acids and those containing ammonium chloride in the place of yeast extract. Biological growth was slower with a lower growth yield in the defined minimal media than in PBBM or CBBM. More butyrate was produced in phosphate-buffered media than in carbonate-buffered media. The bacteria grew without any organic nitrogen in the presence of trace quantities of biotin and pantothenic acid. Anaerobic digester fluid stimulated bacterial growth.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nN'-[2-[[5-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-(2-methylcyclohexyl)-1,2,4-triazol-3-yl]sulfanyl]propanoyl]benzohydrazide (https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/16232686)\nciteturn39search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; PubChem CID: 16232686\n\nPubChem page: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/16232686\n# N'-[2-[[5-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-(2-methylcyclohexyl)-1,2,4-triazol-3-yl]sulfanyl]propanoyl]benzohydrazide\n\nPubChem CID: 16232686\n\nPubChem page: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/16232686\n\n## Names and Identifiers\n\n### Computed Descriptors\n\nProperty Name  | Property Value  | Source\n--- | --- | ---\nIUPAC Name  | N'-[2-[[5-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-(2-methylcyclohexyl)-1,2,4-triazol-3-yl]sulfanyl]propanoyl]benzohydrazide  | PubChem\nInChI  | InChI=1S/C26H31N5O3S/c1-17-9-7-8-12-22(17)31-23(19-13-15-21(34-3)16-14-19)27-30-26(31)35-18(2)24(32)28-29-25(33)20-10-5-4-6-11-20/h4-6,10-11,13-18,22H,7-9,12H2,1-3H3,(H,28,32)(H,29,33)  | PubChem\nSMILES  | CC1CCCCC1N2C(=NN=C2SC(C)C(=O)NNC(=O)C3=CC=CC=C3)C4=CC=C(C=C4)OC  | PubChem\nConnectivity SMILES  | CC1CCCCC1N2C(=NN=C2SC(C)C(=O)NNC(=O)C3=CC=CC=C3)C4=CC=C(C=C4)OC  | PubChem\nMolecular Formula  | C26H31N5O3S  | PubChem\nInChIKey  | LVSBLSSDRBAPQJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N  | PubChem; Computed by InChI 1.07.0 (PubChem release 2024.11.20); Context: An InChIKey is a 27-character hash code derived from an InChI. The International Chemical Identifier (InChI) is a computed, non-proprietary identifier for a chemical structure. The InChI is an International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry (IUPAC) standard. ; Section reference: https://iupac.org/who-we-are/divisions/division-details/inchi/\n\n### Compound Titles\n\n  * N'-[2-[[5-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-(2-methylcyclohexyl)-1,2,4-triazol-3-yl]sulfanyl]propanoyl]benzohydrazide\n\n### IUPAC Names\n\n  * N'-[2-[[5-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-(2-methylcyclohexyl)-1,2,4-triazol-3-yl]sulfanyl]propanoyl]benzohydrazide\n\n##