ion in each mix was brought to 1.16 µM by the addition of the α-³²P dCTP immediately before the sequencing reaction (section 2.2.12.2.2) was initiated.\n\n### 2.2.12.1.2 Others\n\n**Primer:** 2.5 µg/ml New England Biolabs' Synthetic Pentadecamer Primer (5' TCCCAGTCACGACGT 3', see also Sanger et al, 1980) in H₂O. Stored in 50 µl aliquots at -20°C.\n\n**10 × annealing buffer:** 0.1 M Tris, 0.1 M MgCl₂, pH adjusted to 8.0 with 1 M HCl.\n\n**Chase buffer:** 0.5 mM d(A,G,C and T)TP in H₂O. Stored at -20°C.\n\n**Sequencing gel loading buffer:** 10 mM EDTA, 0.3% (w/v) bromophenol blue, 0.3% (w/v) xylene cyanol FF, 98% formamide. Stored at 4°C.\n\n### 2.2.12.2 The sequencing reaction\n\n#### 2.2.12.2.1 Annealing.\n\nEight µl of single stranded M13 template DNA (section 2.2.11.7) was mixed with 1 µl (2.5 ng) primer in 1 × annealing buffer in a 1.5 ml polypropylene Sarstedt tube. The tube was sealed tightly and heated to 60°C for 45 minutes in an oven then allowed to cool to room temperature over 15 minutes.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRapid enrichment of (homo)acetogenic consortia from animal feces using a high mass-transfer gas-lift reactor fed with syngas. (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23732695/)\nciteturn39search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.4 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; # Rapid enrichment of (homo)acetogenic consortia from animal feces using a high mass-transfer gas-lift reactor fed with syngas. ...   * School of Environmental Science and Engineering, Gwangju Institute of Science and Technology (GIST), 261 Cheomdan-gwagiro, Buk-gu, Gwangju, 500-712, Republic of Korea. ... 1999;88(6):682-5; PMID: 16232686\nHence, it is expected that this research could be used as the basis for the rapid enrichment of (homo)acetogenic consortia from various environmental sources.\n\n## MeSH terms\n\n  * Acetates / metabolism\n  * Animals\n  * Bacteria / drug effects\n  * Bacteria / genetics\n  * Bacteria / isolation & purifi